{
  "description": "שליחת לוגים לענן §4 — golden cases of the scrubber. pos-server app/services/log_scrub.py and pos-android mirror it; this file is the same bytes in both repos. For every case: scrub(input) == expected and scrub(expected) == expected.",
  "version": 2,
  "rules": [
    "1 track2: ;? 13-19 digits, = or D, 4+ digits, optional F and ? -> ***",
    "2 secrets: the value of a key (the whole run of [A-Za-z0-9_.-] before [ \\t]*[:=][ \\t]*) -> *** (quotes kept; an unterminated quote runs to the end of the line; a bare value runs to whitespace or one of ,;&\"'(){}[]<>\\ and includes a Bearer/Basic/Token scheme) when the key is secret: split at _ - . and camelCase (aB, 1B, the end of an acronym ABc) and letter/digit boundaries, lower-cased, a token is one of pin|pincode|password|passwd|secret|token|cvv|authorization|apikey, or two tokens in a row are api,key; or the whole key lower-cased is one of token|secret|password|passwd|pin|pincode|cvv|authorization|api_key|apikey|terminal_password. By token, never by substring (pinpadHost, mapping stay). A key that is not secret hides nothing and the search goes on right after it",
    "3 Bearer <token> -> Bearer ***",
    "4 cards: digit groups separated by single spaces or dashes; the leftmost, then longest, window of whole groups that is a card -> ************ + last 4. A card: Luhn, and 13 digits starting with 4; 14 starting with 30|36|38; 15 starting with 34|37; 16-19 any",
    "5 Israeli mobiles: (+972|00972|972|0)[ -]?5X[ -]?XXX[ -]?XX[ -]?XX -> 05X-***-XX + last 2",
    "6 emails: first character + *** + @domain"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "card_contiguous_visa",
      "input": "paid with 4111111111111111 ok",
      "expected": "paid with ************1111 ok"
    },
    {
